<article class="env-lemma" id="0AAF">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AAF">Lemma <span data-tag="0AAF">10.103.10</span>.</a> Suppose $R$ is a Noetherian local ring. Assume there exists a Cohen-Macaulay module $M$ with $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R) = \text{Supp}(M)$. Then for a prime $\mathfrak p \subset R$ we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \dim (R) = \dim (R_{\mathfrak p}) + \dim (R/\mathfrak p).  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows immediately from Lemma <a href="/tag/0AAE" data-tag="0AAE">10.103.9</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>